{#-
  The feed: every world as a card, shown after <main> on every page. It is the one index of worlds
  the site has, and _data/worlds.json is the one place the list and every world's name are kept: a
  world is added, renamed or retired there, and this include, the site map and the mood atlas all
  follow. The site map and the mood atlas used to be the two pages without it, because each listed
  every world itself; those duplicate lists are gone and both pages point at the cards below
  instead, so the shell writes this on every page and has to know nothing about which page it is.

  One flat list, no groups, and no caption: the grid speaks for itself, so its heading is written
  for screen readers only and nothing is said about how many worlds there are or what to do with
  them. Each card carries the world's orientation over its name -- the same phrase the persona
  reads a visitor as -- and the world's own palette, through data-mood (_sass/_mood.scss), so the
  feed is a mosaic of the moods the worlds answer to.

  What the template writes is the whole of what a visitor without scripting gets: a column grid
  of plain cards, every one a link, so the reachability axiom holds and index.html's own markup
  links every world. js/feed.js then lays the cards out as masonry columns, paints each card
  through its module in js/modules/, moves the world the visitor's reading opens onto to the
  front, and keeps dealing fresh cards -- the things the worlds make -- as the visitor scrolls,
  without end. The sentinel at the bottom is what tells it to deal more.
-#}
{%- set here = (page.filePathStem | replace('/', '')) + '.html' if page else '' -%}
<section class='feed' id='feed' aria-labelledby='feed-title'>
  <h2 class='feed-title visually-hidden' id='feed-title'>every world</h2>
  <div class='feed-grid' id='feed-grid'>
{%- for world in worlds.worlds %}
    <article class='card card-world{% if world.file == here %} card-current{% endif %}' data-world='{{ world.file }}' data-mood='{{ world.mood }}' data-name='{{ world.name }}' data-orientation='{{ world.orientation }}'>
      <a class='card-link' href='{{ siteRoot }}{{ world.file }}'{% if world.file == here %} aria-current='page'{% endif %}>
        <div class='card-media' style='aspect-ratio: {{ world.aspect }}'><canvas class='card-canvas' aria-hidden='true'></canvas>{% if world.file == here %}<span class='card-badge'>you are here</span>{% endif %}</div>
        <div class='card-body'>
          <p class='card-overline'>{{ world.orientation }}</p>
          <h3 class='card-title'>{{ world.name }}</h3>
          <p class='card-text'>{{ world.what }}</p>
        </div>
      </a>
    </article>
{%- endfor %}
  </div>
  <div class='feed-sentinel' id='feed-more' aria-hidden='true'></div>
</section>
